HST Office: the user interface is Vietnamese by default on every system, whatever its language
(owner decision 2026-11-10).
- officecfg Linguistic.xcs: the default of /org.openoffice.Office.Linguistic/General/UILocale is
  "vi" instead of empty ("use the desktop's UI language"). It is a schema default, the lowest
  configuration layer: a value in the user's profile (registrymodifications.xcu, written by
  Tools > Options > Languages and Locales > General > User interface or by HST > Ngôn ngữ giao
  diện; empty is "Default", the system's language) and a finalized administrator value win over
  it, and survive updates, which replace only the installation's main.xcd. A profile that never
  chose a language (no stored value) follows the new default. When the vi pack is missing,
  desktop langselect falls back as for "Default" without erasing anything
  (hst-language-selection.patch).
License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_vi_ui_default.py, tests/runtime/check-language-selection.py --phases default.
